---
// The trait score beside the axes the author checked for collateral movement.
//
// One figure, not two, and not a separate tab. This is the Concept Sliders lesson
// verified against the papers: the erasure work shows an edit alongside its effect
// on concepts it did not target, in the same figure. A trait score shown alone
// invites the reader to assume the rest held still.
//
// Two hues carry identity, the targeted trait against collateral axes, not
// magnitude. Bar length already encodes magnitude and colouring by value would
// spend the only free channel restating it.
interface Props {
  trait: number | null;
  coherence: number | null;
  confounds: Record<string, number> | null;
  traitState: string;
  // Whose numbers these are. The tag under the figure used to be unconditional,
  // which was accurate while every number in the corpus was fabricated and became
  // a false caption the moment one was not.
  synthetic?: boolean;
}
const { trait, coherence, confounds, traitState, synthetic = true } = Astro.props;

const rows = [
  ...(traitState === "reportable" && trait !== null
    ? [{ name: "trait", value: trait, targeted: true }]
    : []),
  ...Object.entries(confounds ?? {}).map(([name, value]) => ({
    name, value, targeted: false,
  })),
];

const BAR = 22, GAP = 10, LABEL = 104, TRACK = 300;
const H = rows.length * (BAR + GAP) + 6;
---

{rows.length === 0 ? (
  <p class="note absent-block">
    No confound axes were checked, so nothing here rules out the direction moving
    something other than what its label names. Mean-difference extraction encodes
    sentiment, verbosity or a template artifact as readily as the trait, and an
    unchecked axis is not a passed one.
  </p>
) : (
  <figure class="viz-root chart">
    <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${LABEL + TRACK + 56} ${H}`} role="img"
         aria-label="Trait score beside each confound axis the author measured">
      {rows.map((r, i) => {
        const yTop = i * (BAR + GAP);
        return (
          <>
            <text class="tick" x={LABEL - 10} y={yTop + BAR / 2 + 4} text-anchor="end">
              {r.name}
            </text>
            <rect class="track" x={LABEL} y={yTop} width={TRACK} height={BAR} rx="4" />
            <rect
              class={r.targeted ? "series-1-bg bar" : "series-2-bg bar"}
              x={LABEL} y={yTop} width={Math.max(r.value * TRACK, 3)} height={BAR} rx="4"
            />
            <text class="direct" x={LABEL + Math.max(r.value * TRACK, 3) + 8}
                  y={yTop + BAR / 2 + 4}>
              {r.value.toFixed(4)}
            </text>
          </>
        );
      })}
    </svg>

    <figcaption>
      <span class="key"><span class="swatch series-1-bg"></span>The trait it claims</span>
      <span class="key"><span class="swatch series-2-bg"></span>Collateral axis</span>
      <span class="key">
        coherence {coherence === null
          ? <span class="absent">not measured</span>
          : coherence.toFixed(4)}
      </span>
      {synthetic && (
        <span class="synthetic-tag">synthetic, repeated-digit values</span>
      )}
    </figcaption>

    <p class="note">
      A direction that moves the trait hard and everything else with it is a worse
      artifact than one that moves it modestly and nothing else. These bars are the
      author's own measurements of their own artifact; someone else measuring the
      same axes is under Support cards.
    </p>
  </figure>
)}
